126	/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
127	   BUTTONS  (.ds-btn / .ds-btn-primary / .ds-btn-secondary)
128	   ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
129	   Two variants, ONE construction. Primary and secondary share:
130	     - dimensions (padding 10px 20px, font-size 14px / weight 600)
131	     - shape (border-radius 6px)
132	     - 1.5px transparent border, with the actual color carried by a
133	       linear-gradient painted on the border-box via the dual-background
134	       technique. Lighter at the top, darker at the bottom — "lit from
135	       above." Solid hex colors (not low-opacity tints), so the hue stays
136	       unambiguous regardless of what's behind the button.
137	     - an equal-on-all-sides inner vignette (inset 0 0 6px) that softly
138	       darkens the perimeter so the surface doesn't read as flat. Center
139	       of the button stays the canonical fill color.
140	     - a soft outer drop shadow that grounds the button on the page.
141	
142	   Hover direction: BRIGHTEN, not darken. Primary fill lightens
143	   (#a5d6fe → #c2e2ff); secondary fill stays at #ffffff (already maximum
144	   brightness) but the inner vignette nearly vanishes so the surface
145	   reads as cleaner / more luminous. Border deepens slightly for visual
146	   feedback. Outer drop shadow does not change on hover.
147	
148	   Pressed: 1px drop via translateY, outer drop removed, vignette
149	   deepened, border gradient flattened to a single mid-tone (no
150	   "lit from above" read anymore).
151	
152	   Why the dual-background trick: a single `border-color` can't carry a
153	   vertical gradient. We use two backgrounds — one clipped to
154	   padding-box (the fill) and one to border-box (the border gradient) —
155	   with `border: 1.5px solid transparent` so the gradient shows through.
156	   Follows border-radius correctly; universal browser support.
157	
158	   Naming and usage:
159	     .ds-btn                Base shell (always applied).
160	     .ds-btn-primary        Open Blue fill, blue gradient border.
161	     .ds-btn-secondary      White fill, warm-grey gradient border.
